# {{.ServiceName}}

Generated with KPro's unified `service` profile.

API and Message-transport selection is declared in `kpro.service.yaml`.
Contracts live under `api/`, generated bindings under `internal/`, and
application-owned implementations beside those bindings. Process lifecycle
stays in `cmd/{{.ServiceName}}`; endpoint assembly is generated under
`internal/kproapp`.

```bash
go mod tidy
kpro validate
kpro generate --check
go run ./cmd/{{.ServiceName}}
```

The create-once files `internal/kproapp/http.go`, `grpc.go`, and `message.go`
contain protocol-native defaults whenever their API is selected. They are safe
to edit. `internal/kproapp/endpoints.gen.go` is generator-owned and is refreshed
from `kpro.service.yaml`.

HTTP defaults to `:8080`, gRPC to `:9090`, and Message transports use their
documented scaffold ports. Protobuf regeneration requires `protoc`,
`protoc-gen-go`, and `protoc-gen-go-grpc` on `PATH`; pin their versions in CI.
QUIC requires reviewed TLS material through `KPRO_QUIC_CERT_FILE` and
`KPRO_QUIC_KEY_FILE`; the scaffold never creates or commits a private key.

Generated files are replaced only while they still match the generation lock;
create-once implementation and mount files remain safe to edit. Review all
timeout, capacity, TLS, authentication, persistence, and observability settings
for the target workload before deployment.
